# Commander PoE HAT (rev H0) - the mainboard's PoE converter on a small board of its own, for a stock
# Radxa ZERO 3E used as the codec core.  The ZERO 3E keeps its own RJ45: the PoE voltage leaves it on its
# 4-pin PoE header, this board turns it into 5 V, and the 5 V goes back in through the 40-pin header.
# The converter itself (sheet poe) is the mainboard's 30_poe.net, listed in shared.txt.
SHEET hatif

# --- PoE input: 4-wire lead to the ZERO 3E's PoE header (PRIMARY side, up to 57 V) ---
# All four taps go through the diode bridges on the poe sheet, so the order and the polarity of the four
# wires do not matter.
J60 HDR1x4G:POE_TAPS 1=TR0_48V 2=TR1_48V 3=TR2_48V 4=TR3_48V

# --- 5 V to the ZERO 3E: 2x20 header, for a 40-way ribbon cable or a direct stacking socket ---
# Only the supply pins are used: 5 V on 2 and 4, ground on the eight ground pins.  The 3.3 V pins and every
# signal pin are left open, so the cable can be a full 40-way ribbon or a cut-down one covering pins 1-10.
# F60 protects the cable (two 28 AWG ribbon wires carry the 5 V).
J61 HDR2x20:ZERO3E_40PIN 2=VCC5V_ZERO 4=VCC5V_ZERO 6=GND 9=GND 14=GND 20=GND 25=GND 30=GND 34=GND 39=GND
NC J61 1 3 5 7 8 10 11 12 13 15 16 17 18 19 21 22 23 24 26 27 28 29 31 32 33 35 36 37 38 40
F60 PTC:3A VOUT_5V VCC5V_ZERO
C601 22uF VCC5V_ZERO GND
C602 100nF VCC5V_ZERO GND
TP60 TP VCC5V_ZERO

# --- 5 V to the rest of the Commander (hub strip, bays): 2 pins 5 V, 2 pins ground ---
J62 HDR1x4G:5V_OUT 1=VOUT_5V 2=VOUT_5V 3=GND 4=GND

# --- "PoE power present" indicator ---
R601 1K VOUT_5V LED_PWR_A
D60 LED:GREEN A=LED_PWR_A K=GND
